<div class="legacy-fb5ec070f2"><h2>NRA BASIC SHOTGUN SHOOTING COURSE</h2></div>
<p>
</p><div class="legacy-fb5ec070f2"><b>COURSE GOAL:</b>To teach the basic knowledge, skills and attitude necessary for the safe and proper use of a shotgun in shooting a moving target.</div>
<table role="presentation" class="legacy-2dda5cd5ef">
<tbody><tr><td><b>Length of Course: 10 hours</b>
<br><br>
<b>Course Lessons:</b>
<div class="legacy-list">
Lesson I: Shotgun Knowledge and Safe Handling
</div>
<div class="legacy-list">
Lesson II: Ammunition Knowledge and the Fundamentals of Shotgun Shooting
</div>
<div class="legacy-list">
Lesson III: Firing the First Shoot
</div>
<div class="legacy-list">
Lesson IV: Shotgun and Shooting Skills Practical Exercise
</div>
<div class="legacy-list">
Lesson V: Shotgun Games and Activities
</div>
</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<br>
<br>
<div class="legacy-fb5ec070f2"><b>Special Note:</b> The purpose of this course is to teach basic shotgunning skills. It is neither designed nor intended to teach the actual sports of skeet or trap or similar activities.</div>
